<%# The threads panel lives in a host container, not next to the editor. Bali renders
    nothing inside `#panel-de-hilos` —React portals that— so the mode flag has to travel
    with the portal. If it does not, the reply box and the actions menu show up here even
    when `:read_only` was asked for. %>
<div class="flex gap-4">
  <%# `min-w-0`: the editor carries a minimum width of its own, and without this the
      growing column refuses to shrink and the panel runs off the screen. %>
  <div class="grow min-w-0">
    <%= render Bali::BlockEditor::Component.new(
          editable: editable,
          comments: comments,
          comments_container_id: 'panel-de-hilos',
          initial_content: content
        ) %>
  </div>

  <aside id="panel-de-hilos"
         class="bn-mantine w-80 shrink-0 border-l border-base-300 overflow-y-auto p-4">
  </aside>
</div>
